#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74ea3255-015a-50b0-8024-a8bd10ccce6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)+\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350601} {:answer/id #uuid "1971a81d-2780-5fa0-9d86-ca7187751f0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350602} {:answer/id #uuid "694b4e0f-cdc4-5864-99af-a4f8021b36eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350603} {:answer/id #uuid "ef46e9b2-fb80-5352-ae7f-121c2b560095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350604} {:answer/id #uuid "15a039fa-b24d-53f0-ad8f-546ce55f387c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15a039fa-b24d-53f0-ad8f-546ce55f387c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350605} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b3a3094-9cc4-50a6-ac66-ab505d122bb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f0ca935-919b-51f7-aa7b-48465faaebbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-340465" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x-x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x+x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160927bb-68f5-5755-9362-1d2f5420ea1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)-\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350608} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fde45f-7710-5109-9934-6ec671fe1832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350609} {:answer/id #uuid "078dd2f5-6d1e-5134-ab23-ed8b80666df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350610} {:answer/id #uuid "6557a9b2-406d-5c7b-a4ac-73aed9cc88f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350611} {:answer/id #uuid "2689ca25-b3e2-51bc-8390-a64123e1a99e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(18x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6557a9b2-406d-5c7b-a4ac-73aed9cc88f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350611} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9485bf-03c7-57c2-a876-30440191b722" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0a429ad-91a6-5abe-8ae3-10dad144b5c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340469" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x-5x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x+5x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(18x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(18x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{36}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a30dcf0d-0f76-5d3a-b32b-108df2a695dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350615} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4aa282-27e1-5c47-a1f7-b6542b141886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350616} {:answer/id #uuid "a3588672-ee56-53fb-a422-c9dd388971cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350617} {:answer/id #uuid "db194638-5b4c-52e4-aaa5-6c75ca627fc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350618} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd7ed29-9cc8-5ea5-b120-ef340c8d0c22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad4aa282-27e1-5c47-a1f7-b6542b141886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350616} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa59035-ab11-51e1-826f-e48aecb8774a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be5333ee-0a3d-563b-a5e4-ba1cb1a4c8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340479" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x+3x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x-3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0422f2eb-7f61-5e23-bd00-f566513e6b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350622} {:answer/id #uuid "09d2d64b-31b4-5e58-b3b2-f6b0ae12a527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350623} {:answer/id #uuid "f28ce658-1195-57f7-8bde-b60d8abf3d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350624} {:answer/id #uuid "8daa46b2-5323-58b0-a420-761f3efb2179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350625} {:answer/id #uuid "815b0c61-439a-5054-89dd-76ead181b0e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09d2d64b-31b4-5e58-b3b2-f6b0ae12a527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350623} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc00f90-f685-5365-b535-2af958bcdb13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a135a1df-aa0e-5ea6-9580-c700cdbdf03a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340483" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x+5x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x-5x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e2c3ce8-147a-54d0-9b78-d30c68e2288b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e2c3ce8-147a-54d0-9b78-d30c68e2288b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350629} :answer-field/id #uuid "6effd691-5287-5b89-9f0d-92c8725847d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb756ef7-080e-5245-8c3b-08721c6ba08e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340505" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-8x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+8x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{22}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(1-0)-\\frac{1}{22}(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{55}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
